-- title:
--   The fixed field K₀ is the level field F₀ (q=3)
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q=3$ and $M'$ a non-zero natural number with $q\nmid M'$ (hypothesis `hqM'`). A guard prime $\ell_g$ is fixed with $\ell_g\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g\mid M'$ (`hℓg`, `hℓg12`, `hℓgM'`). Further, $\ell$ is a prime with $\ell\ge 3$, $\ell\ne q$, $\ell\nmid M'$ (`hℓ`, `hℓ3`, `hℓq`, `hℓM'`).
--
--   The subgroup $H_1\le(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ is, by `hH₁`, the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22) — the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$ — with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/\ell_g)^\times$; so $H_1$ consists of the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$ and modulo $\ell_g$. Two function fields of Laurent series are involved: `fieldBar q M'`, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((\mathsf q))$ generated by the images of the $q$-expansions of the modular functions of level $\Gamma_{H}(q^2M')$ for $H=$ `levelH q M'`, and `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield generated by the images of the field $\mathbb Q\big(\mathsf q\mapsto \mathsf q^{d},\ d\mid M'\big)$-expansions `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` (generated over $\mathbb Q$ by the series `qExpand ℚ d jq` for $d\mid M'$); `hle` asserts `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'`.
--
--   On the arithmetic side, $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $(q)\in A^{\mathrm{nonunits}}$ (`hA`, the predicate `LiesOverPrime`), $W$ is a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over the residue field of $A$ which, by `hW`, is exactly the set `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)` of supersingular places (rational, affine geometric places $w$ with $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the generator `jGeomGen` lying in `ssJSet q`, the set of $j$-invariants all of whose elliptic curves have trivial $q$-torsion), and $s$ is a distinguished element of $W$. Here `R₀` is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` (a valuation subring of integers, a surjective residue map with kernel the maximal ideal, a map on places preserving degrees and orders, and compatibility with $A$ and with `residue A`), and `hR₀` demands that the residue map of `R₀` on Laurent series arising from $A$ agrees with coefficientwise reduction $A\to$ `ResidueField A`.
--
--   The field of constants is an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\mathbb Q\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$; write $A_0$ for the contraction `A.comap (algebraMap ↥k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))`. Elements $\pi_0,\zeta_0,\varpi_t,\xi\in k_0$ are fixed, with $\pi_0\in A$ (`hπ`). The group `hdvr`–`hκ` of hypotheses on constants requires: $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, Henselian, with algebraically closed residue field, and every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0\cap A$. Further: $\zeta_0$ is a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity (`hζ₀`); $\varpi_t\in A$ and $\varpi_t^{q^2-1}=q\,u$ for a unit $u$ of $A$ (`hϖtA`, `hϖt`); $\xi$ is a primitive $q$-th root of unity (`hξ`); $\ell_g-1$ is a unit of $A_0$ (`htame`, tameness). An intermediate field $K_b$ of $k_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $K_b=\bot$ (`hKb`) carries a valuation subring $A_b$ contracting to $A$ (`hAb`) with maximal ideal generated by a non-zero $\varpi_b$ (`hϖb`, `hϖb0`).
--
--   The rigid-level field is an intermediate field $K_\ell$ of $k_0\subseteq k_0((\mathsf q))$, equal by `hKℓ` to the base change to $k_0$ of the level-$\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ function field `xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁`, and it is an algebra over $A_0$ compatibly with $k_0$. Its chart data are: a non-zero $j_\ell\in K_\ell$ which is the coefficientwise image of the $j$-expansion `jq` (`hjℓ`); the chart algebra `chartAlgFin A₀ Kℓ jℓ` of elements of $K_\ell$ integral over $A_0[j_\ell]$; a maximal ideal $y$ of that algebra containing $\pi_0$ (`hy`, `hϖy`) which is supersingular, in the sense that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism from the chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$ the image of `jChartFin` lies in `ssJSet q Ω` (`hss`); an $A_0$-subalgebra $B_t$ and a valuation subring $W_t$ of $K_\ell$ with $B_t\subseteq W_t$ (`hBW`); natural numbers $n,m$ with $1\le n\mid q+1$ and $1\le m$ (`hn1`, `hnq`, `hm1`); an element $\varpi_t'\in A_0$ with $\varpi_t'=\varpi_t$ (`hϖt'`) and $\pi_0^m=\varpi_t'\cdot(\text{unit})$ (`hm`); an element $\zeta_c$ of the adic completion of $A_0$ which is an $n$-th root of unity all of whose non-trivial powers have $\zeta_c^k-1$ a unit (`hζc`, `hζcprim`); the fact `hjK` that `jqNModC k₀ q` lies in $K_\ell$, together with `hjC` that it lies in the chart algebra and `ha₀y` that its difference from the constant $a_0\in A_0$ lies in $y$; a finite set `ends` of subrings of $K_\ell$; and $\gamma_0\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ with a $k_0$-automorphism $\tau_0$ of $K_\ell$ which is a level automorphism at $\gamma_0^{-1}$ in the sense of `IsLevelAutAt ↥k₀ q ξ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ₀⁻¹ Kℓ τ₀` (the condition that for all ratios $f/g$ of modular forms of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions, and all embeddings $\iota:k_0\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota(\xi)=e^{2\pi i/q}$, the coefficientwise image of $\tau_0$ applied to $f/g$ is the ratio of the $q$-expansions of $f$ and $g$ translated by $\gamma_0^{-1}$ conjugated by the $q$-dilation), preserving $W_t$ (`hγ₀Γ`, `hγ₀Γ0`, `hτ₀`, `hτ₀W`).
--
--   The remaining hypotheses fall into named groups. `hover` states that $y$ lies over the place $s$: for every $g\in$ `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose image lies in the integers of `R₀`, which has no pole at any place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` where $j$ has none, and whose `R₀`-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, and for every constant $c\in k_0\cap A$ whose residue in `ResidueField A` equals the value of that residue at $s$, the difference between $g$ (read in the chart algebra) and $c$ lies in $y$. `hOrbit` states that every maximal ideal $y'$ of the chart algebra containing $\pi_0$ and satisfying the same lying-over property as in `hover` is carried to $y$ by some level automorphism: there are $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving the chart algebra with $b\in y\iff\tau b\in y'$. The hypothesis `hS1` (fourteen clauses, summarised here) is the rigid-chart package: the chart algebra is contained in $B_t$, $K_\ell$ is the fraction field of $B_t$, $B_t$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_0$ with $B_t/(\pi_0)$ of Krull dimension at most $1$; $W_t$ contracts to $A_0$ on $k_0$, is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ and is the localisation of $B_t$ at that maximal ideal, and $y$ is the contraction of the maximal ideal of $W_t$ to the chart algebra; for every algebra structure of `GaloisField q 2` on the residue field of $A_0$ there is a surjection $\rho$ from $B_t$ onto [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) of that residue field, with kernel the maximal ideal of $W_t$, compatible with constants, and equivariant for the level automorphisms through an element $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,c)$ of [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) acting by [`DrinfeldCurve.hAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L325), the scalar $c$ being non-trivial for non-trivial $\tau$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and being also realised by a level automorphism with trivial matrix part; and $B_t$ is stable under the level automorphisms for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, every prime of $B_t$ containing $\pi_0$ is a level-automorphism translate of the one cut out by $W_t$, and $\pi_0$ divides any element of $B_t$ all of whose translates lie in the maximal ideal of $W_t$. The hypothesis `hR7` (twelve clauses, summarised here) is the deck-group-and-ends package: $\tau_0^n$ is the identity on $B_t$ while no smaller power is, every level automorphism preserving $W_t$ agrees on $B_t$ with a power $\tau_0^k$ with $k<n$; `ends` has exactly $q+1$ elements, the level automorphisms permute them, act transitively on them, fix each of them when equal to $\tau_0$, and distinct ends are separated by an element which is a unit in one and not in the other; there is a finite-type $A_0$-subalgebra $B_c$, stable under the level automorphisms, contained in every end with each end a localisation of it; an end mapped into $W_t$ by a level automorphism forces that automorphism to preserve $W_t$; each end $O$ is contained in $W_t$, is local and noetherian, contains the chart algebra, contracts to $A_0$ on $k_0$, has every element congruent to a constant modulo a non-unit, and its adic completion is identified by a ring isomorphism $\iota$ with the crossing model `UVCrossingModel` of the adic completion of $A_0$ at $\pi_0^m$ (the two-variable power series ring modulo $X_0X_1-\pi_0^m$), in such a way that constants go to constants, two elements $c_x,c_y$ of $O$ with $c_xc_y=\pi_0^m\cdot(\text{unit})$ go to unit multiples of the coordinates $U$ and $V$, $c_y$ lies in and $c_x$ outside the maximal ideal of $W_t$, the difference `jqNModC k₀ q` $-\,a_0$ goes to a unit times $V^e$ with $e\ge1$, and $\tau_0$ is implemented by an automorphism $\theta_0$ of the crossing model scaling $U$ by $\zeta_c$ and $V$ by $\zeta_c^{-1}$ modulo the square of the maximal ideal; each end moreover carries a valuation subring $W_x$ of $K_\ell$ (containing $O$ and the chart algebra, contracting to $A_0$, a discrete valuation ring with uniformiser $\pi_0$, with a non-reduction property for polynomials evaluated at a parameter and at `jqNModC k₀ q`, with $c_x$ in and $c_y$ outside its maximal ideal, cutting out $y$ on the chart algebra, and detecting the end among all ends) and a finite-type $A_0$-subalgebra $B_x$ of $B_t\cap O$, stable under the level automorphisms, with no poles where $j_\ell$ has none, with $O$ its localisation, and containing an element outside every valuation subring of $K_\ell$ which contracts to $A_0$, is non-reducing at $j_\ell$ and fails to contain $O$; finally, a valuation subring of $K_\ell$ contracting to $A_0$, containing the chart algebra and cutting out $y$ either contains $B_t$ or is dominated by an end. The hypothesis `hR9` provides an element of $B_t$ lying outside every valuation subring of $K_\ell$ which contracts to $A_0$, has $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal and is non-reducing on monic polynomials evaluated at $j_\ell$; `hR10` provides, for every maximal ideal $y''$ of the chart algebra containing $\pi_0$ that is not the image of $y$ under any level automorphism, an element of $B_t$ separating the two in every valuation subring as specified. Finally `hn` fixes $n=2\cdot$ `placeWidthChar q M' s`, which for $q=3$ is twice $6$ or twice $1$, according as the $j$-value of $s$ is $0$ or not, divided by the ramification index `placeRamificationJ M' s`.
--
--   The descent data are: $G$, the subgroup of $k_0$-automorphisms of $K_\ell$ generated by all level automorphisms at $\gamma^{-1}$ for $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ (`hG`); $K_0=K_\ell^{G}$, the fixed field of $G$ (`hK₀`); the $A_0$-subalgebra $B_0$ of $G$-invariants of $B_t$ (`hB₀`); and the valuation subring $W_0'$ of $K_0$ obtained by contracting $W_t$ (`hW₀'`).
--
--   With `fieldBar q M'` regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $k_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$, the conclusion asserts: for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $k_0\subseteq$ `fieldBar q M'` such that an element of `fieldBar q M'` lies in $F_0$ if and only if every one of its Laurent coefficients lies in (the image of) $k_0$, there exists a $k_0$-algebra isomorphism $\varphi:K_0\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }F_0$ with the following three properties.
--
--   First, $\varphi$ is coefficientwise base change: for every $f\in K_0$, applying `coeffMap` of the inclusion $k_0\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$ to the Laurent series of $f$ yields the Laurent series of $\varphi(f)$.
--
--   Second, $\varphi$ transports level automorphisms to the automorphisms `levelAutBar`: for every $\zeta\in$ `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$), every primitive $q$-th root of unity $\xi'\in k_0$ with $\zeta$ equal to the image of $\xi'$, every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every $k_0$-automorphism $\tau$ of $K_\ell$ satisfying `IsLevelAutAt ↥k₀ q ξ' q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ Kℓ τ` — note that here the matrix is $\gamma$, whereas the generators of $G$ are the level automorphisms at $\gamma^{-1}$ — the automorphism $\tau$ maps $K_0$ into itself, and for every $f\in K_0$ one has $\varphi(\tau f)=$ `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` applied to $\varphi(f)$.
--
--   Third, $\varphi$ is the identity on level-$M'$ modular functions: for every $g\in$ `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose coefficientwise image `coeffEmb ↥k₀ g` lies in $K_\ell$ and in $K_0$, the value of $\varphi$ at it equals the image of `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) g`, viewed in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, under the inclusion of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` into `fieldBar q M'` given by `hle`.
--
--   This is the descent step identifying the $G$-fixed field of the rigid-level field $K_\ell$ with the level field $F_0$ cut out inside `fieldBar q M'` by the condition that all Laurent coefficients be constants, together with the dictionary between level automorphisms upstairs and the automorphisms `levelAutBar` downstairs and the normalisation on level-$M'$ modular functions; it is stated at $q=3$ in the $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$ frame, with the parameters and clauses of the rigid-chart package listed as explicit binders. It combines the two cited descent statements and is used by the assembly theorem [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_linkedInertia_of_rigidChart_of_eq_three_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_linkedInertia_of_rigidChart_of_eq_three_of_dvd).
